{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR DESIGN CONSTRAINT (verbatim):\n\n\"compaction needs to work in environments without local cron and CI. that's why the original\ndesign was linked to an operation.\"\n\nThis is a real gap in what I have built, and I did not see it. Story A removed the\noperation-linked trigger (compact-on-close) and change 1717 replaces it with a GitHub Actions\nschedule — which is OUR repo's infrastructure. An adopter running rebar as a library or CLI\nwith no CI and no local cron now has NO compaction trigger at all: their event logs would grow\nwithout bound, and nothing in the product would ever fold them. I optimised for this repo and\ncalled it \"the store's only standing trigger\" without asking what a store outside this repo\nwould do.\n\nThe scheduled sweep is still right as the amortized path where CI exists. What is missing is a\nFLOOR that works everywhere: an operation-linked trigger that does not reintroduce the 13m53s\nlock hold story A removed.\n\nRequired shape (operator-specified design space):\n- after a covered write completes and RELEASES the store lock (close being the natural\n  candidate), check the two-arm selection cheaply;\n- if work exists, run the fold out-of-band from the session's perspective — either a detached\n  local worker, or inline but with fold-outside-lock discipline: fold with NO lock held, then\n  take the lock only for the rename+commit, with a re-check.\n\nOperational nuance to respect: the detached-worker pattern already exists in this codebase as\n`enrich_drain._spawn_detached_drain`. Reuse its shape — including the stamped-lock discipline\njust fixed in change 1704 — rather than inventing a third dialect.\n\nThe ticket must NOT close with the CI-less gap open."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786613529750492001,"uuid":"4c25c140-ab58-44d3-8ec2-ef9c30457c43"}